@startuml circuit-breaker
title Circuit breaker on every synchronous call between services (Resilience4j)
hide empty description

[*] --> Closed
Closed : calls go through,
Closed : the last 10 calls are counted
Open : the called service is not called,
Open : the caller answers 503 at once
HalfOpen : one trial call goes through

Closed --> Open : half of the last 10 calls failed\n(timeout, 5xx, no connection)
Open --> HalfOpen : 30 s passed
HalfOpen --> Closed : the trial call succeeded
HalfOpen --> Open : the trial call failed

legend bottom
  Set up in application.yml of the caller, one named instance per called service; the called service knows nothing about it.
  4xx answers are not failures: the called service works.

  | Caller | Called service | Answer when open |
  | individuals-api | person-service | 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE |
  | individuals-api | transaction-service | 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE |
  | transaction-service | currency-rate-service | 503 RATE_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE |

  Metrics of every instance go to /actuator/prometheus by themselves: resilience4j_circuitbreaker_state,
  resilience4j_circuitbreaker_failure_rate, resilience4j_circuitbreaker_calls, resilience4j_circuitbreaker_not_permitted_calls.
  Grafana: a panel per caller and an alert when a breaker is open.

  Not used: Kafka (asynchronous, the outbox resends), Keycloak service token (cached, renewed rarely).
end legend
@enduml
